    "expected_outcome": "Cal CV RMSE for the SG+SNV+Ridge grid should be lower than the Raw Ridge reference and comparable to or better than the Whittaker variant, with the retained alpha chosen by train_cv_rmse. I expect the smoothing step to matter more than the alpha sweep. Figures are predictions only; actual Cal CV and the sealed Validation RMSE will be reported after execution.",
    "expected_revision": 1,
    "observations": [
      {
        "claim": "Cal profile (n=28, 12 wavelengths, regular axis) shows high_frequency_noise (0.580) and low_signal_to_noise tags, with mild scatter_variation (0.209); baseline drift (0.092) and spikes (0.0) are low, so smoothing and scatter handling are the relevant levers, not iterative baselines or despiking.",
        "evidence_refs": [
          "profile:calibration",
          "task:user"
        ]
      },
      {
        "claim": "Official method cards for sg_smooth and whittaker_smooth explicitly target high_frequency_noise / low_signal_to_noise with project-bounded window/lambda candidates; SNV targets additive+multiplicative scatter with no tunable hyperparameters.",
        "evidence_refs": [
          "method:sg_smooth:a7560c9ec34f2dd9",
          "method:whittaker_smooth:e545c6375cd36e7e",
          "method:snv:3ffad76b24481338"
        ]
      },
