        "claim": "Budget allows at most 2 grid candidates, 3 frozen CV folds and 7 total fits (2*3+1), so the parameter search must be minimal.",
        "evidence_refs": [
          "budget:session",
          "protocol:sealed_holdout"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "phase": "initial",
    "rationale": "The profile tags point to high-frequency noise and low SNR as the main obstacles and scatter as secondary, so a smoothing step plus scatter correction is the most defensible ordered pipeline. I chose SG smoothing (window=7, order=2) because it is the retrieved method explicitly matching high_frequency_noise/low_signal_to_noise with project-bounded candidates, and a modest window limits peak distortion on the short 12-wavelength axis. SNV is added because it is hyperparameter-free and directly matches scatter_variation at negligible cost. Ridge with an internal scaler is a low-variance linear estimator suited to 28 samples and 12 collinear variables without demanding a baseline family override. I selected the grid variant (2 alphas) rather than fully fixed because a single regularization sweep is cheap within budget and can capture under/over-regularization, while Whittaker and Raw references provide meaningful structural comparisons. No mandatory baseline family is imposed.",
